{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgC2PB1dbJT83YgpbUcbp", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I fixed the bug and all 3 tests now pass (`python3 -m unittest -v`).\n\n**The bug:** discounts were divided by 100 twice. `discounts.lookup()` already returns a fraction (`0.10` for 10%), and `invoice_total()` in `invoice/totals.py` divided that by 100 again. So \"WELCOME10\" took off 0.1% instead of 10%, and the total came out as 117.88 instead of 106.20.\n\n**The fix:** `invoice_total()` now uses the fraction directly: `amount * (1 - discount)`. I renamed the variable from `percent_off` to `discount`, since the old name suggested a percentage and probably led to the extra division.\n\nI changed the calling code rather than `lookup()` because `lookup()`'s docstring says it returns a fraction, and `invoice_total()` is the only place that calls it.\n\nI haven't committed the change."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 964, "cache_read_input_tokens": 18568, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 964}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "57e495de-2e67-4b9c-8638-c30a5f93c02e", "uuid": "c012ae0e-afd7-4a41-bc93-5767031f3bf5", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T17:54:36.367Z", "request_id": "req_011CgC2PAS99XWE5VJgDpNs5"}
